<title>USA: Lubrizol Q1 oper shr $0.66 vs $0.59.</title>
<headline>Lubrizol Q1 oper shr $0.66 vs $0.59.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>THE LUBRIZOL CORPORATION</p>
<p>			CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF INCOME</p>
<p>							Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								March 31</p>
<p> (In Thousands Except Per Share Data)	    1997	1996</p>
<p> Net sales					    $387,749 $405,412</p>
<p> Royalties and other revenues			1,260    1,689</p>
<p>   Total revenues				    389,009  407,101</p>
<p> Cost of sales					 258,107  273,595</p>
<p> Selling and administrative expenses	    40,014   40,608</p>
<p> Research, testing and development expenses   34,982   40,696</p>
<p>	     Total cost and expenses	     333,103  354,899</p>
<p> Gain on investments					--   53,280</p>
<p> Other income - net				    3,245    3,213</p>
<p> Interest - net					(1,578)  (1,978)</p>
<p> Income before income taxes			 57,573  106,717</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			 18,712   35,481</p>
<p> Net income					     38,861   71,236</p>
<p> Net income per share				    .66     1.14</p>
<p> Average number of common shares outstanding  58,504   62,615</p>
<p>NOTE: Consolidated net income in the first quarter of 1996 was $71.2 million and included an after-tax gain of $34.6 million from the sale of investments. Excluding the 1996 investment gain, earnings per share for the first quarter of 1997 increased 12 percent over last year's first quarter net income of $.59 per share.</p>
<p>Lubrizol repurchased 290,000 of its common shares during the first quarter leaving 2.2 million shares remaining on its current authorization.</p>
<p>The company said the first quarter, 1997 was strong as operating earnings per share increased 12 percent despite a $.02 per share negative impact from the stronger U.S. dollar.</p>
</text>
